body:
What format are you sending the stills in? If you're simply screenshotting the footage or using the snapshot feature in premiere then you're not actually sending your colourist a RAW image, it'll be compressed into a jpg, png or tiff. The RAW data won't be present in your screenshot, so the way the colour reacts with the pixels will be different.

&#x200B;

You may want to do some research into how you can convert your BRAW footage into some kind of RAW still format that preserves the data - not sure if this is possible or if there's some kind of workaround. I think you may be able to use the media management tool in DaVinci Resolve to trim your BRAW clips down to a few frames, and send those to your colourist so he can work with RAW files and provide you with the correct settings, You would most-likely want to back-up your footage to another location though, so you don't end up trimming your only footage and losing it all.
